# Fable of the Mirror-Breaker, chapter II is a "may": Bot1 chooses no card, so nothing is discarded and nothing is drawn
# (the hand stays Island, Swamp, Plains and the turn-3 Forest). Then chapter I's Goblin Shaman token ("Whenever this token
# attacks, create a Treasure token.") attacks Bot2 on turn 3: a Treasure arrives and Bot2 takes 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Fable of the Mirror-Breaker
Island
Swamp
Plains
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Fable of the Mirror-Breaker.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Choose()
Bot1.Attack(Goblin Shaman Token > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Island; Swamp; Plains; Forest
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Fable of the Mirror-Breaker; Goblin Shaman Token; Treasure Token
Bot2.Life = 18
